-- title:
--   The full Fourier integral of the truncation discrepancy is zero
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ne0$, let the finite CFZ-family index type have decidable equality, and fix a smooth sieve cutoff $\chi$, natural $W,b$, and $R\ge2$. The integral of the canonical carry truncation discrepancy over the full paired Fourier coordinate spaces is zero. No coprimality or good-prime hypothesis is required.
